---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import icon from '@assets/logo.svg';
import icon_name from '@assets/logo_name.svg';
import LineBreak from "@components/LineBreak.astro";
---

<header>
	<div class="menu">
		<a id="a-intro">About</a>
		<a id="a-practical-information">Practical information</a>
		<!--<a id="a-program">Program</a>-->
		<a id="a-sponsors">Organizers</a>
	</div>
	<div><a class="icon" id="a-title" style="padding: 0"><Image src={icon_name} alt="XRTransitions"/></a></div>
	<div>
		<a class="button" id="a-application-process">
			Call for Papers
		</a>
	</div>
</header>
<div id="container">
	<section id="title">
		<Image src={icon} alt="RJC IHM 2026" class="rjc-logo"/>
		<h1>Collaborative XRTransitions</h1>
		<h2>The First International Workshop on the Multiple Dimensions of the Transitions in Collaborative eXtended Reality</h2>
	</section>

	<section id="intro">
		<h3>Workshop Motivation & Scope</h3>
			<p>
The number of collaborative systems in extended reality scenarios has considerably increased these last years, using shared spaces, tasks or objects that blur the boundaries between physical and digital life. Collaborative XR environments have many applications, for example in the fields of education, training, industrial manufacturing, design, architecture, and urban planning. These applications define varied, sometimes dynamic, collaborative situations. Multiple dimensions of collaborative situations have been explored depending on the number of users involved, the nature of the tasks to be performed, the manipulated objects, and the characteristics of the environment.
			</p>
			<br>
			<p>
Collaborative XR environments often require users to adapt to changing tasks, roles, spatial arrangements, interaction modalities, and levels of immersion. Designing efficient transitions between these collaborative situations is therefore essential for maintaining users’ awareness, coordination, communication, and overall engagement. However, the definition of seamless and efficient transitions between collaborative situations still remains underexplored. Indeed, while transitions and transitional interfaces are key concepts in the study of single-user cross-reality systems (see the scoping survey on Cross-reality Systems by Auda et al. https://doi.org/10.1145/3616536), the design of transitions within collaborative situations has not been studied in a systematic manner. A better understanding of such transitions could improve the continuity, usability, and effectiveness of collaborative XR experiences across a wide range of applications.
			</p>
			<br>
			<p>
The XRTransitions ISMAR workshop aims to explore the multiple dimensions of the transitions between collaborative situations. The key difference with single-user situations is the number of involved users in the collaborations: there are many possibilities for releasing the transitions, depending on which user(s) start it and which user(s) execute it. The workshop aims to discuss the multiple dimensions of collaborational transitions : 			</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					Users
				</li>
				<li>
					Duration (automatic/smooth,long, short)
				</li>
				<li>
					Devices (physical/virtual, multi-sensory)
				</li>
			</ul>
	</section>

	<section id="practical-information">
		<h3>Important dates</h3>
		<div id="dates">
			<ul>
				<li><strong>June 1st:</strong> Submissions Open</li>
				<li><strong>August 30th:</strong> Submissions Deadline</li>
				<li><strong>September 30th:</strong> Acceptance Notification</li>
				<li><strong>November 30th to December 4th:</strong> RJC IHM 2024</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section id="topics">
		<h3>Topics of Interest</h3>

	</section>

	<LineBreak/>
	<section id="application-process">
		<h3>Submission Guidelines</h3>
		<p>
			Submissions must follow the IEEE VGTC formatting guidelines and will be peer-reviewed based on relevance, originality, and contribution diversity. XRStand invites full-length and short‐format papers (up to 4 pages, excluding references). Acceptable formats include:
		</p>
		<ul>
			<li>Research Papers: describing novel XR work with an explicit standardization angle.</li>
			<li>Survey & Vision Papers: overviews of existing XR standards, taxonomies, or roadmaps.</li>
			<li>Position papers: reflecting on a conceptual challenge in XR standardization.</li>
			<li>Project papers: reports on community-driven or industry-led standardization efforts.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>All accepted papers (up to 4 pages, excluding references) will be published in the ISMAR 2025 Abstracts & Workshop Proceedings and made available via the IEEE Xplore Digital Library. At least one author from each accepted submission must register for the workshop and present their work at XRStand.
		</p>

		<h4>Formatting</h4>
		<p>
			All submissions should be 4 pages of length excluding references, and use the IEEE VGTC formatting template and be submitted in PDF format. Submissions must be original, unpublished, and not currently under review elsewhere. Papers that fail to comply with formatting or length limits will be desk-rejected.
		</p>

		<h4>Review Process</h4>
			<p>
				All the submissions will be single blind and reviewed by the workshop organizers and program committee. Each submission will undergo peer review by at least two domain experts. Accepted manuscripts will be accepted as posters, and all presenters are expected to give a lightning talk before their poster presentation. Acceptance does not restrict future publications authors may present extended or modified versions of their work as full papers, short papers, or journal articles, provided they include significant new contributions beyond the original workshop submission. The review criteria will include but not limited to Originality; relevance to workshop themes; technical rigor or conceptual clarity; potential impact on XR community.
			</p>
			<br>
			<p>
			Review decisions are final. Authors of accepted papers will need to submit a revised version that addresses the feedback provided in the reviews before official acceptance to the workshop.
			</p>

		<h4>Submission Site</h4>
		<p></p>
	</section>

	<LineBreak/>
	<section id="organizers">
		<h3>Organizers</h3>
		<h4>General Chairs</h4>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<a href=" https://adrienchaffangeon.xyz/">Adrien Chaffangeon Caillet</a> (Grenoble INP, France)
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href="https://people.irisa.fr/Maud.Marchal/">Maud Marchal</a> (Univ. Rennes, INSA, IRISA, France)
			</li>
			<li>
				<a href=" https://iihm.imag.fr/nigay/">Laurence Nigay</a> (Université Grenoble Alpes, France)
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h4>Program Committee</h4>

	</section>

</div>

<script>
	function changeCss () {
		let headerElement = document.querySelector("header");
		if (headerElement === null) return
		window.scrollY > 10 ? headerElement.classList.add("shadow") : headerElement.classList.remove("shadow")
	}
	window.addEventListener("scroll", changeCss , false);

	function scrollToId (name: string) {
		let element = document.getElementById(name);
		if (element === null) return
		window.scrollTo(
			{
				top: Math.max(0, element.getBoundingClientRect().top-80),
				left: 0,
				behavior: "smooth",
			})
	}
	document.getElementById("a-intro")
		?.addEventListener("click", () => scrollToId("intro"))
	document.getElementById("a-practical-information")
		?.addEventListener("click", () => scrollToId("practical-information"))
	document.getElementById("a-program")
		?.addEventListener("click", () => scrollToId("program"))
	document.getElementById("a-sponsors")
		?.addEventListener("click", () => scrollToId("organizers"))
	document.getElementById("a-title")
		?.addEventListener("click", () => scrollToId("title"))
	document.getElementById("a-application-process")
		?.addEventListener("click", () => scrollToId("application-process"))

</script>

<style>
	#container {
		font-family: Inter, Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Arial Nova', 'Nimbus Sans', Arial, sans-serif;
		min-height: 100%;
		max-width: 1200px;
		margin: auto;
		padding-bottom: 150px;
	}

	main {
		height: 100%;
		display: flex;
		justify-content: center;
	}

	h1 {
		font-size: 2em;
		margin-top: 0.25em;
		margin-bottom: 0.25em;
	}

	header {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 45% 10% 45%;
		padding: 20px 60px;
		background: white;
		font-family: Inter, Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Arial Nova', 'Nimbus Sans', Arial, sans-serif;
		position: sticky;
		top: 0;
		transition: 0.5s;
	}

	header.shadow {
		box-shadow: rgba(60, 64, 67, 0.3) 0px 1px 2px 0px, rgba(60, 64, 67, 0.15) 0px 1px 3px 1px;
		transition: 0.5s;
	}

	header div:nth-child(2) {
		justify-self: center;
	}

	header div:nth-child(3) {
		justify-self: end;
	}

	header img {
		width: 200px;
		height: auto;
	}

	#title{
		text-align: center;
		margin-top: 10px;
		margin-bottom: 20px;
	}

	#title h1 {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	#title h3 {
		margin-top: 0;
		font-weight: normal;
		font-size: smaller;
		color: gray;
	}

	#dates ul, #organizers ul {
		margin-left: 0;
		margin-top: 7px;
		padding-left: 0;
		list-style-type: none;
	}

	#links, #sponsor-logo-container {
		display: flex;
		gap: 16px;
		width: 90%;
		margin: 0 auto;
	}

	img.sponsor-logo {
		height: 50px;
		width: auto;
		margin: 0 25px;
	}

	header a {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		padding: 10px 12px;
		color: #1f1f1f;
		text-decoration: none;
		transition: color 0.2s;
	}

	header a:hover {
		color: #e86d15;
		font-weight: bolder;
	}

	header a svg {
		height: 1em;
		margin-left: 8px;
	}

	a.button {
		color: white;
		background: linear-gradient(160deg, #f3bb54 0%,#c55ca3 50%, #5a62ac 100%);
		box-shadow:
			inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.12),
			inset 0 -2px 0 rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.24);
		border-radius: 10px;
	}

	a.button:hover, header a.button:hover {
		transition: 600ms;
		color: #000000;
		font-weight: normal;
		box-shadow: none;
	}

	a.icon {
		font-weight: bold;
		font-size: large;
	}

	pre {
		font-family:
			ui-monospace, 'Cascadia Code', 'Source Code Pro', Menlo, Consolas, 'DejaVu Sans Mono',
			monospace;
		font-weight: normal;
		background: linear-gradient(14deg, #d83333 0%, #f041ff 100%);
		-webkit-background-clip: text;
		-webkit-text-fill-color: transparent;
		background-clip: text;
		margin: 0;
	}

	h2 {
		margin: 0;
		font-weight: normal;
		color: #111827;
		font-size: 20px;
	}

	h3 {
		margin-top: 10px;
		margin-bottom: 5px;
		font-weight: initial;
		font-size: 2em;
		color: #343333;
	}

	h4 {
		margin-top: 20px;
		margin-bottom: 5px;
		font-weight: initial;
		font-size: 1.5em;
		color: #343333;
	}


	p {
		color: #4b5563;
		font-size: 16px;
		line-height: 24px;
		letter-spacing: -0.006em;
		margin: 0;
		text-align: justify;
	}

	code {
		display: inline-block;
		background:
			linear-gradient(66.77deg, #f3cddd 0%, #f5cee7 100%) padding-box,
			linear-gradient(155deg, #d83333 0%, #f041ff 18%, #f5cee7 45%) border-box;
		border-radius: 8px;
		border: 1px solid transparent;
		padding: 6px 8px;
	}

	.box {
		padding: 16px;
		background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 1);
		border-radius: 16px;
		border: 1px solid white;
	}

	.rjc-logo {
		max-width: 80%;
	}

	#program-container {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 110px repeat(5, auto);
	}

	#program-container .classe {
		background: rgb(138 215 245);
	}

	#program-container .break {
		background: rgb(245 231 138);
	}

	#program-container .workshop {
		background: rgb(139 214 90);
	}

	#program-container .other {
		background: rgb(245 138 165);
	}

	#program-container .activity {
		background: rgb(241 138 245);
	}

	#program-container .orga {
		background: rgb(222 222 222);
	}

	#program-container div div {
		border-top: 1px solid lightgray;
		border-left: 1px solid lightgray;
		padding: 5px;
	}

	#program-container #program-friday div {
		border-right: 1px solid lightgray;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(1) {
		height: 20px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(2) {
		height: 20px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(3) {
		height: 60px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(4) {
		height: 20px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(5) {
		height: 60px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(6) {
		height: 20px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(7) {
		height: 80px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(8) {
		height: 60px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(9) {
		height: 20px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(10) {
		height: 60px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(11) {
		height: 20px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(12) {
		height: 40px;
	}

	#program-container div div:nth-child(13) {
		height: 20px;
		border-bottom: 1px solid lightgray;
	}

	.mobile-time {
		display: none;
	}

	@media screen and (max-width: 1200px) {
		header {
			grid-template-columns: 50% 50%;
			padding: 20px 30px;
		}

		header div:nth-child(2) {
			justify-self: start;
			text-align: left;
		}
		.menu {
			display: none;
		}
	}

	@media screen and (max-width: 900px) {
		#container, #program-container {
			display: flex;
			flex-direction: column;
		}

		#container {
			padding: 20px;
		}

		#program-container #program-time, #program-container .empty {
			display: none;
		}

		.mobile-time {
			display: initial;
			font-weight: bold;
		}

		#program-container > div {
			margin-bottom: 10px;
		}

		#program-container div div {
			max-width: 400px;
			height: auto;
			margin: auto;
		}

		 a.button {
			padding: 14px 18px;
		}

		h1 {
			line-height: 1.5;
		}
	}
</style>
